                <pb facs="0148" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg802"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure to inclosure 6 in No.
                        228.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract in regard to the jurisdiction of German
                        consuls</hi>.</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Section</hi> 17.</p>
                <p>“Every consul has the right to issue police-rules, with binding power, for those
                    persons who are under his jurisdiction, and to levy a fine not exceeding thalers
                    10 ($7) in case of non-compliance.</p>
                <p>“These rules have to be transmitted to the legation, or to the minister for
                    foreign affairs. The envoy plenipotentiary, as well as the minister for foreign
                    affairs, have the right to annul the police laws of the consular court.”</p>
            </div>
